  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 1,
  "sortOrder": 21001,
  "verseCount": 18,
  "aliases": [
    "Eccl",
    "Ecc",
    "Qoheleth"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The words of the Preacher, the son of David, king in Jerusalem.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Vanity of vanities, saith the Preacher, vanity of vanities; all is vanity.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "What profit hath a man of all his labour which he taketh under the sun?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "One generation passeth away, and another generation cometh: but the earth abideth for ever.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "The sun also ariseth, and the sun goeth down, and hasteth to his place where he arose.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "The wind goeth toward the south, and turneth about unto the north; it whirleth about continually, and the wind returneth again according to his circuits.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "All the rivers run into the sea; yet the sea is not full; unto the place from whence the rivers come, thither they return again.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "All things are full of labour; man cannot utter it: the eye is not satisfied with seeing, nor the ear filled with hearing.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "The thing that hath been, it is that which shall be; and that which is done is that which shall be done: and there is no new thing under the sun.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Is there any thing whereof it may be said, See, this is new? it hath been already of old time, which was before us.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "There is no remembrance of former things; neither shall there be any remembrance of things that are to come with those that shall come after.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "I the Preacher was king over Israel in Jerusalem.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "And I gave my heart to seek and search out by wisdom concerning all things that are done under heaven: this sore travail hath God given to the sons of man to be exercised therewith.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "I have seen all the works that are done under the sun; and, behold, all is vanity and vexation of spirit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "That which is crooked cannot be made straight: and that which is wanting cannot be numbered.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "I communed with mine own heart, saying, Lo, I am come to great estate, and have gotten more wisdom than all they that have been before me in Jerusalem: yea, my heart had great experience of wisdom and knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "And I gave my heart to know wisdom, and to know madness and folly: I perceived that this also is vexation of spirit.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "For in much wisdom is much grief: and he that increaseth knowledge increaseth sorrow.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Ecclesiastes 1:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:ecclesiastes:1:18"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
